## Held by lints

- No bare words in a template: every string goes through t(), nine languages measured in their own fonts, each label in its own slot
- No import cycles; an app never imports another app without saying why, and the list of the shares only shrinks
- Chunk budgets as tripwires: growth is fine when it buys simplicity, and a chunk that shrinks lowers its own budget
- Generated outputs are never edited by hand; a stale one fails the build, and the script that writes it says which
- The kernel names no window, no document, no navigator and no storage, so it runs under node as it is
- Every command is reachable from a key, a bar or the palette, and none is bound twice at one place
- Every template is written back by the kernel byte for byte, and its plain link reads back as itself
- Every document the skill shows is one of an app's own templates
